WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:03.730
Home Alone is undeniably a Christmas classic.

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.340
How could anyone not love it?

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:10.060
It tells the story of a young boy, Kevin McCallister,
who's accidentally left behind when his family

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.710
leaves for a Christmas vacation.

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:16.170
To make matters worse, two burglars have targeted
the McCallister house while Kevin is there

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.200
by himself.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.100
Unfortunately, that's also where things kind
of start to break down.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.869
Kevin defends his homestead by setting up
a series of elaborate and dangerous traps

00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:29.560
in order to stop the bad guys from robbing
the place...instead of, you know, calling

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:30.810
the cops.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:35.559
And that's just one of many of the dumb things
in Home Alone that everyone just ignored.

00:00:35.559 --> 00:00:36.559
Call the police

00:00:36.559 --> 00:00:41.539
What's the first thing that every kid learns
to do when they realize they're in danger?

00:00:41.539 --> 00:00:46.059
"Didn't they teach you that in school about
911 that you call if somebody needs help?"

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:46.640
"Yep."

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:47.640
"Yaaa"

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:51.739
Either Kevin didn't get the memo, or he just
doesn't have the mental capacity of a four-year-old.

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:56.359
Sure, the phone lines are down, but he knows
how to get into town to go food shopping,

00:00:56.359 --> 00:01:00.019
and he knows exactly when Harry and Marv will
be robbing his house.

00:01:00.019 --> 00:01:04.510
Kevin only dials 911 near the end of the film,
after the crooks have made their way through

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:06.750
almost all of his traps.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:12.250
Even weirder, when he finally calls the cops,
he disguises his voice and tells them his...neighbor's

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.250
address?

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:14.680
Why was that the plan?

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:19.400
Did he think the cops would hear a child's
voice calling for help on 911 and they wouldn't

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.550
come?

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.500
Or maybe it's because...

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.220
The cops in this town suck

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:28.720
"Well he's just home alone and I would like
somebody to go over to the house and see that

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.770
he's alright just to check on him."

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:35.230
"You want us to go to your house just to check
on him?"

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:38.800
The cops of Home Alone are basically garbage
with badges.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.070
When they're informed about a small child
left without supervision, they send one police

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:45.070
officer to the McAllister house.

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:49.670
The cop knocks on the door and then arbitrarily
decides Kevin's mom just can't keep track

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:51.850
of her children because no one answers.

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:55.409
Maybe that's why the Wet Bandits don't seem
concerned in the slightest when Kevin makes

00:01:55.409 --> 00:01:57.369
multiple threats to call the police.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:58.240
"Hey!

00:01:58.460 --> 00:01:59.440
I'm calling the cops!"

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.200
"Wait wait wait wait wait he wants us to follow
him.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.570
I got a better idea come on."

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:09.109
Harry and Marv simply ignore Kevin and continue
to invade his home.

00:02:09.109 --> 00:02:12.650
They're already guilty of breaking and entering,
and they're attempting to assault a minor,

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:17.600
so the charges would probably be pretty severe,
but because Kevin lives in a town full of

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.430
Paul Blarts, there's really no reason for
them to worry.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:23.319
Even the pizza boy has lost hope

00:02:23.319 --> 00:02:28.609
Home Alone must happen in some dystopian alternate
reality where the law simply doesn't matter.

00:02:28.609 --> 00:02:32.930
When Kevin plays the audio from an old gangster
movie to make the pizza guy think he's about

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:37.050
to get murdered, there are absolutely no consequences.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:40.130
(gunshots)

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:44.260
Apparently, this kid just went back to delivering
more pizzas and never warned anyone about

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:49.230
the spray of gunfire that just took out half
of the neighborhood's inflatable Santas.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:51.700
Marv doesn't know how TV works

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:56.549
The pizza boy scene is weird, but Kevin uses
the same trick on Marv as he tries to break

00:02:56.549 --> 00:02:58.069
in the back door.

00:02:58.069 --> 00:03:02.139
It worked on the especially stupid pizza boy
because Kevin only played certain parts of

00:03:02.139 --> 00:03:06.269
the conversation, making the pizza boy believe
that he was talking to a real person.

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:08.370
And we all know that pizza boys are dumb.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:11.400
"People said I was dumb, but I proved them!"

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.700
But when Marv comes to the door, Kevin just
plays the movie.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:19.780
Sure, Kevin adds his own special effects,
but has Marv never heard a TV before?

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.230
How does this work?

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:22.669
Why is this happening?

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:25.599
"Is this real life?"

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:27.859
Uncle Frank is a monster

00:03:27.859 --> 00:03:31.599
So we've talked about how the movie's suburban
hellscape is filled with morons.

00:03:31.599 --> 00:03:37.950
But we can't let Kevin's clan off the hook:
the McCallister family is a bunch of hot garbage.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:42.329
While it makes sense that Kevin might get
picked on by his older siblings and cousins,

00:03:42.329 --> 00:03:46.329
why are the adult McCallisters straight up
bullying an eight-year-old?

00:03:46.329 --> 00:03:51.200
When it comes to the steaming pile of awful
human trash that is this family, Uncle Frank

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.379
lives at the top.

00:03:52.379 --> 00:03:56.790
When Kevin gets into a fight with Buzz — who
was pretending to throw up on Kevin, by the

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:00.079
way — some soda gets spilled on Uncle Frank's
lap.

00:04:00.079 --> 00:04:02.739
Kevin didn't even do it; it was Kevin's useless
dad.

00:04:02.739 --> 00:04:05.170
So, naturally Uncle Frank loses it.

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:07.670
"Look what you did, you little jerk!"

00:04:09.359 --> 00:04:13.590
Nobody defends Kevin, not his parents, and
not even the kid from Pete &amp; Pete.

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:15.889
"Kevin, you're such a disease."

00:04:15.889 --> 00:04:20.570
Frank is a middle-aged adult with some very
deep psychological issues.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:25.560
Forget Harry and Marv, if anyone deserves
a nail through the foot, it's Frank.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:28.590
The McCallisters may all be monsters

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:32.270
Kevin's mom has to rush back home because
they can't get in touch with anybody to look

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:35.290
in on Kevin, but how is that possible?

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:38.250
The entire town didn't go away for Christmas.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:41.470
Kevin goes to school and even mentions that
he has friends.

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:45.820
So why can't his parents call one of their
families, or any of the friends of Kevin's

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.950
seven thousand siblings?

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:52.120
Is there literally no one in the entire state
of Illinois that the McCallisters can trust

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:53.201
to check up on Kevin?

00:04:53.201 --> 00:04:56.220
Kevin is going to kill his family

00:04:56.220 --> 00:05:00.010
Remember how Harry and Marv kept falling down
the stairs because they were covered with

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:01.010
ice?

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:03.880
Or how the basement steps were covered in
tar and nails?

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:08.760
Kevin's massive family was basically walking
into a death trap by the end of the movie.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:12.700
Kevin isn't exactly the most conscientious
kid, and he's even pretty happy about the

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.530
possibility that he's psychically murdered
them...

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:18.320
"I made my family disappear."

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:22.410
...so it's incredibly unlikely that the kid
cleaned up after himself.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:25.780
Hopefully, Uncle Frank cracks his melon on
those icy steps first.

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.230
"Hey pizza's here!"

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:29.640
"Here you go, that's $122.50."

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.490
"Uh it's my brother's house he'll take care
of it."

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:33.490
"Your name's Kevin?

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.700
You know what they're gonna call you in France
don't you huh?"

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:37.460
"No."

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:38.600
"Yank!"

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:40.080
Ugh.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:41.720
We really hate that guy.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:42.940
Thanks for watching!

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.860
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.970
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

